      "names": [
        "controlled timing: host boundaries, finite huge and fractional delays never become early actions",
        "controlled timing: independently literal nanosecond boundaries forbid fractional and long early firing",
        "controlled timing: cancellation, chunk replacement and renewal cannot renew the absolute limit",
        "controlled lifetime: strengthening before and during confirmation preserves the final bound and first failure",
        "controlled lifetime: every owned stdio error keeps the first error and finalizes once before owner rejection",
        "controlled worker handback: final facts survive exit/error order, uncertainty and final-observer failure",
        "controlled lifetime: launch errors, repeated postlaunch child errors and close guards remain distinct",
        "controlled lifetime: disposal errors preserve publication cut and detach only at natural stream close",
        "controlled lifetime: callback errors stop ordinary observations and retain the first error",
        "controlled lifetime: no launch, close without exit, probe errors and Windows scope stay distinct",
        "controlled lifetime: synchronous calls return fresh recomputed snapshots while one sealed completion never changes",
        "controlled lifetime: re-entrant signal notices strengthen or finish the attempt and no obsolete signal follows",
        "controlled lifetime: first error and disposal faults are recorded before the one completion publication",
        "controlled lifetime: exit and close re-entering a probe seal both entered assessments and drop its stale result",
        "controlled lifetime: exit re-entering a probe drains its nested absence and rejects the stale result before close",
        "controlled lifetime: immediate strengthening inside a probe keeps its tightened bounds and drops the stale graceful result",
        "controlled lifetime: a re-check requested inside a kill probe leaves that probe current and its KILL bound intact",
        "controlled lifetime: exit inside the first immediate probe keeps KILL and its bound before handback and drops the stale result",
        "controlled lifetime: an immediate request completed by nested absence, exit and close is not resurrected by its stale result",
        "controlled lifetime: ordinary, throwing and fast-path assessments count at entry; a probe cancelled before entry is not counted",
        "controlled helper continuation: uncertainty preserves diagnostics and stops dependent launches, reads and publication",
        "controlled command continuation: unresolved cleanup stops before expected-report reads and preserves first error",
        "controlled owners: command and HTTP reject the original stream error before reports or a dependent request",
        "physical lifetime: actual direct exit, stdio close, disposal and group absence are separately observed",
        "physical HTTP owner: response, invalid/missing port, failed request and exceptional owner path finalize",
        "physical owner capture: finite inherited-pipe late output stays HTTP diagnostic and never worker/command result",
        "controlled lifetime: both long grace phases and final drain recheck their exact monotonic bounds",
        "physical lifetime: an escaped finite pipe holder is outside owned-group absence and drain remains bounded"
